  "description": "Serilog sink that ships log events to TAF Kibana via the TAF.Kibana.SDK. Version 1.2.9 adds a per-line poison cap to DrainAsync (KibanaSinkDefaults.MaxBufferReplayAttempts = 5): a permanently-rejected payload is dropped after the threshold instead of pinning the file forever and starving newer entries. Counter is in-memory (resets on process restart), keyed by line content, pruned at end of each drain to bound memory growth. Pair with TAF.Kibana.SDK 1.2.5 which fixes the upstream cause where missing UserId on bulk-log payloads produced the 400 cascade in the first place. Version 1.2.8 fixed a DiskBuffer drain livelock where eviction-during-drain resurrected lines from the snapshot. Version 1.2.7 closed a DiskBuffer drain-vs-append race, made ExtractGuid accept ScalarValue(Guid) and (string), and added a once-per-minute LogWarning escalation when GroupByTenant drops events for missing TenantId/AppId. Provides batched delivery, disk-buffer resilience, secret scrubbing, and BusContext-aware tenant routing.",
